      "classification": "Exact intended Rustls resolution already present upstream; not migrated.",
      "observation_and_limit": "Old patch changes Rustls 0.23.45 to 0.23.46 with registry checksum 48e13bd8c0e9365c43cfa5c9e8f9ad49d3c8444926c9aac819e0e4dc503c8fdf and refreshes its Bazel metadata. Selected upstream Cargo manifest and lock already select 0.23.46 with that checksum; MODULE.bazel.lock contains rustls_0.23.46 and no rustls_0.23.45 key. The historical patch need not be copied to establish that resolution. This does not claim that every current Rustls advisory is resolved or replace step-7 latest-stable discovery."
    },
    {
      "path": "patches/openai/codex/security-RUSTSEC-2026-0367/zip-security-update.patch",
      "blob": "c27a71514a193817c6b3efd4f6bcfbfe21b59b10",
      "sha256": "e4b081ffc35d58ca955ea83379374b328cf61a555c4b3c65767d58c789ff3c37",
      "classification": "Step-7 ZIP update and compatibility-review candidate; old major-version migration not replayed.",
      "observation_and_limit": "Old patch changes ZIP 2.4.2 to 9.0.4, adapts plugin-reader APIs, preserves then-default compression features, adds a libbz2-rs-sys license allowance and rebases a zstd-sys dependency overlay. Selected upstream already uses ZIP 9.0.0 with explicit compression features and default-features=false. Its plugin extraction handles entry.name() as a fallible result and contains no old ZipFile helper signature. Resolve the then-latest stable ZIP and actual remaining compatibility changes during step 7; preserve current feature choices, regenerate dependency metadata and investigate any demonstrated overlay need separately. Old patch audit/test claims are historical, not fresh acceptance."
    }
